FLUTED PANEL — MODELLING PLAN (surface draft; to be refined)
Metres unless stated; values in braces are this object's parameters. Z up, floor at Z 0. Hosted on a wall segment: local X runs along the segment, origin at its midpoint on the centre-line.

WHAT IT IS
fluted timber feature wall, warm oak, vertical rhythm, contemporary hotel

GEOMETRY
Model the object described above as clean, closed meshes with real thickness and small bevels on exposed edges (about 2 mm) so highlights catch. Drive every dimension from these parameters:
- Panel length: {length}
- Panel height: {height}
- Bottom above floor: {baseOffset}
- Flute pitch: {flutePitch}
- Flute profile: {profile} (one of: Half-round / Square / Tapered / V-groove)
- Flute depth: {fluteDepth}
- Gap between flutes: {fluteGap}
- Backer thickness: {backerThk}
- Shadow gap at ends: {shadowGap}
- Facets per round flute: {sides}
- Cutout (TV / niche): {cutout}
- Cutout width: {cutoutWidth}
- Cutout height: {cutoutHeight}
- Cutout centre height: {cutoutCentre}
- Rotation (deg): {rotation}
- Anchor Direction: {anchorDir} (one of: Top-Left / Top-Center / Top-Right / Left-Center / Center / Right-Center / Bottom-Left / Bottom-Center / Bottom-Right)
- Margin from host: {margin}
- Flip side: {flipSide}
Keep the proportions of a well-made real product; add the secondary detail a close-up render needs (joints, reveals, fixings) but no hidden interior geometry.

MATERIALS
- Base colour: {baseColor}
- Roughness: {roughness}
Principled BSDF per visible part, using the colour and roughness above for the main surface; secondary parts in a neutral complementary finish. Use Object / box-projected texture coordinates (no UVs needed). Add a subtle noise bump (strength ~0.03) so surfaces are not perfectly flat.

LIGHTS
None. This object does not emit light.

CHECKS (measure after building)
- Panel length = {length}
- Panel height = {height}
- Flute depth = {fluteDepth}
- Cutout width = {cutoutWidth}
- Cutout height = {cutoutHeight}
- All meshes closed, no duplicate faces, origin as stated above.
